      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What you're describing is the terrifying emptiness that comes when the scaffolding of your life collapses. You're not just sad; you're facing a void where your self used to be. Instead of trying to \"navigate\" this wreckage, maybe you could just allow yourself to stop moving entirely. A small, quiet act of self-caring—like just letting yourself rest or letting the pain wash over you without fighting it—is a valid, necessary step.",
      "source": "target",
